{"$schema":"folio-archimate-normalised/v1","id":"id-dthsc-overlay-0-1-0-draft-1","name":"DTH-SC overlay on the DPI-H reference architecture","file":"0.1.0-draft.1/dth-sc-overlay.archimate","documentation":"Overlay of dth-sc on smart-ra ArchiMate 0.3.0-draft.1: the five architecture variants of the supply chain DTH (Figs 15-19). Elements tagged overlay:base are reference copies of smart-ra elements (the IRI names the original); elements tagged overlay:owner=dth-sc are added by this DTH and are not part of smart-ra. Built by scripts/archimate/build_variant_views.py.","properties":[],"elements":[{"id":"id-e7af3fb7d601d3758195e19bfa9474cf","type":"ApplicationComponent","name":"Inventory Management System","layer":"Application","documentation":"Inventory management below the central warehouse, at district and facility level (DTH SC Figs 18-19). Close to smart-ra's Health Facility Logistics Management System; kept as its own element until the owner decides (dth-sc#2).","properties":[{"key":"overlay:owner","value":"dth-sc"}],"folder":["Application"]},{"id":"id-57be342b728e5ac08fa2143faba83984","type":"ApplicationComponent","name":"Cold Chain Management System","layer":"Application","documentation":"DHSC architecture framework, Fig. 14 (PDF 34-35)","properties":[{"key":"overlay:base","value":"https://litlfred.github.io/smart-ra/archimate/0.3.0-draft.1/elements/id-57be342b728e5ac08fa2143faba83984.jsonld"}],"folder":["Application","smart-ra (base, reference copies)"]},{"id":"id-a5808a3c23e755509c26c634b21cda83","type":"ApplicationComponent","name":"Data Repositories","layer":"Application","documentation":"Global or regional data repositories that aggregate master or transactional data (e.g., product master data and serialization data). (PDF 34-35)","properties":[{"key":"overlay:base","value":"https://litlfred.github.io/smart-ra/archimate/0.3.0-draft.1/elements/id-a5808a3c23e755509c26c634b21cda83.jsonld"}],"folder":["Application","smart-ra (base, reference copies)"]},{"id":"id-2158ff0de2f95b2cbe005c3bf6fc9c01","type":"ApplicationComponent","name":"Data Warehouse","layer":"Application","documentation":"DHSC architecture framework, Fig. 14 (PDF 34-35)","properties":[{"key":"overlay:base","value":"https://litlfred.github.io/smart-ra/archimate/0.3.0-draft.1/elements/id-2158ff0de2f95b2cbe005c3bf6fc9c01.jsonld"}],"folder":["Application","smart-ra (base, reference copies)"]},{"id":"id-370b6bdcb29449c9be74644ffacc94aa","type":"ApplicationComponent","name":"Dispensing System","layer":"Application","documentation":"The ability to record the act of preparing and giving stock to a patient or consumer. This includes the list of minimums that any system providing direct distribution of medical goods should be able to provide for.","properties":[{"key":"overlay:base","value":"https://litlfred.github.io/smart-ra/archimate/0.3.0-draft.1/elements/id-370b6bdcb29449c9be74644ffacc94aa.jsonld"}],"folder":["Application","smart-ra (base, reference copies)"]},{"id":"id-5f6d9b9678824b37b95952735420ae8d","type":"ApplicationComponent","name":"Facility registry","layer":"Application","properties":[{"key":"overlay:base","value":"https://litlfred.github.io/smart-ra/archimate/0.3.0-draft.1/elements/id-5f6d9b9678824b37b95952735420ae8d.jsonld"}],"folder":["Application","smart-ra (base, reference copies)"]},{"id":"id-38e8733e58775142ab2abec1b563131d","type":"ApplicationComponent","name":"Finance and Insurance Systems","layer":"Application","documentation":"Finance and insurance systems that combine data from the dispensing system with individuals' information to verify and process insurance claims. (PDF 35)","properties":[{"key":"overlay:base","value":"https://litlfred.github.io/smart-ra/archimate/0.3.0-draft.1/elements/id-38e8733e58775142ab2abec1b563131d.jsonld"}],"folder":["Application","smart-ra (base, reference copies)"]},{"id":"id-4f7d1037d878435aa3a0fbdcee0c685b","type":"ApplicationComponent","name":"Forecasting & Supply Planning System","layer":"Application","documentation":"Capture and analyze data on demand, inventory levels, open purchase orders, and pending replenishments to forecast and plan future needs, across programs and levels of care. Demand Planning involves forecasting future requirements based on historical patterns and anticipated future conditions. Supply Planning applies constraints including funding availability, procurement mechanisms, stock-on-hand, and lead times to develop executable plans that meet those needs.","properties":[{"key":"overlay:base","value":"https://litlfred.github.io/smart-ra/archimate/0.3.0-draft.1/elements/id-4f7d1037d878435aa3a0fbdcee0c685b.jsonld"}],"folder":["Application","smart-ra (base, reference copies)"]},{"id":"id-e3c4f0ec36f35eccb0d4c50f887316e5","type":"ApplicationComponent","name":"Global Platforms","layer":"Application","documentation":"Global platforms developed by funders or procurement agencies. (PDF 35)","properties":[{"key":"overlay:base","value":"https://litlfred.github.io/smart-ra/archimate/0.3.0-draft.1/elements/id-e3c4f0ec36f35eccb0d4c50f887316e5.jsonld"}],"folder":["Application","smart-ra (base, reference copies)"]},{"id":"id-d626508a7dc55b1fb11bf34f57f8ddd9","type":"ApplicationComponent","name":"Health Management Information System","layer":"Application","documentation":"DHSC architecture framework, Fig. 14 (PDF 34-35)","properties":[{"key":"overlay:base","value":"https://litlfred.github.io/smart-ra/archimate/0.3.0-draft.1/elements/id-d626508a7dc55b1fb11bf34f57f8ddd9.jsonld"}],"folder":["Application","smart-ra (base, reference copies)"]},{"id":"id-80856538cbd44167a37b276e38c994c3","type":"ApplicationComponent","name":"Interoperability Component","layer":"Application","properties":[{"key":"overlay:base","value":"https://litlfred.github.io/smart-ra/archimate/0.3.0-draft.1/elements/id-80856538cbd44167a37b276e38c994c3.jsonld"}],"folder":["Application","smart-ra (base, reference copies)"]},{"id":"id-f8c43d85b20e5671b613d723483217a8","type":"ApplicationComponent","name":"Manufacturer Systems","layer":"Application","documentation":"DHSC architecture framework, Fig. 14 (PDF 34-35)","properties":[{"key":"overlay:base","value":"https://litlfred.github.io/smart-ra/archimate/0.3.0-draft.1/elements/id-f8c43d85b20e5671b613d723483217a8.jsonld"}],"folder":["Application","smart-ra (base, reference copies)"]},{"id":"id-f6022dce920d4f828581dd2f7e15280f","type":"ApplicationComponent","name":"Order Management System","layer":"Application","documentation":"Manage the process of capturing, approving, allocating and tracking the requests against inventory.","properties":[{"key":"overlay:base","value":"https://litlfred.github.io/smart-ra/archimate/0.3.0-draft.1/elements/id-f6022dce920d4f828581dd2f7e15280f.jsonld"}],"folder":["Application","smart-ra (base, reference copies)"]},{"id":"id-58832f74225140c38ddc4ebaa5fef90c","type":"ApplicationComponent","name":"Procurement Management System","layer":"Application","documentation":"Managing the creation, processing, and invoicing of the purchase orders and the visibility into the fulfillment progress.","properties":[{"key":"overlay:base","value":"https://litlfred.github.io/smart-ra/archimate/0.3.0-draft.1/elements/id-58832f74225140c38ddc4ebaa5fef90c.jsonld"}],"folder":["Application","smart-ra (base, reference copies)"]},{"id":"id-59c26d672a4248e0bb83cf4d26cba10c","type":"ApplicationComponent","name":"Product Registry","layer":"Application","properties":[{"key":"overlay:base","value":"https://litlfred.github.io/smart-ra/archimate/0.3.0-draft.1/elements/id-59c26d672a4248e0bb83cf4d26cba10c.jsonld"}],"folder":["Application","smart-ra (base, reference copies)"]},{"id":"id-1555c26cfbcd57f49b6e63fed8491d80","type":"ApplicationComponent","name":"Quality Systems","layer":"Application","documentation":"Laboratory or quality monitoring systems that integrate with HSCISs to trigger alerts on quality issues or trigger product quarantines or recalls. (PDF 35)","properties":[{"key":"overlay:base","value":"https://litlfred.github.io/smart-ra/archimate/0.3.0-draft.1/elements/id-1555c26cfbcd57f49b6e63fed8491d80.jsonld"}],"folder":["Application","smart-ra (base, reference copies)"]},{"id":"id-22eff58eae365a4f8d0e0368d8c3497e","type":"ApplicationComponent","name":"Regulatory Systems","layer":"Application","documentation":"Regulatory systems that combine supply chain data from the dispensing system with health information and individuals' data to conduct post-market surveillance and pharmacovigilance, or use supply chain data to perform product recalls. (PDF 35)","properties":[{"key":"overlay:base","value":"https://litlfred.github.io/smart-ra/archimate/0.3.0-draft.1/elements/id-22eff58eae365a4f8d0e0368d8c3497e.jsonld"}],"folder":["Application","smart-ra (base, reference copies)"]},{"id":"id-566242a824b24ede92c7b6593b827b94","type":"ApplicationComponent","name":"Supplier & Contract Management System","layer":"Application","documentation":"Managing sourcing and contracting strategies, handling tender management, and tracking supplier performance.","properties":[{"key":"overlay:base","value":"https://litlfred.github.io/smart-ra/archimate/0.3.0-draft.1/elements/id-566242a824b24ede92c7b6593b827b94.jsonld"}],"folder":["Application","smart-ra (base, reference copies)"]},{"id":"id-199c0717881f4992970d6ba85780b74e","type":"ApplicationComponent","name":"Supplier registry","layer":"Application","properties":[{"key":"overlay:base","value":"https://litlfred.github.io/smart-ra/archimate/0.3.0-draft.1/elements/id-199c0717881f4992970d6ba85780b74e.jsonld"}],"folder":["Application","smart-ra (base, reference copies)"]},{"id":"id-ba1ec21bae4641378c56f714f72042d7","type":"ApplicationComponent","name":"Transportation Management System","layer":"Application","documentation":"Managing the process of route management, transportation execution, freight audit and payment.","properties":[{"key":"overlay:base","value":"https://litlfred.github.io/smart-ra/archimate/0.3.0-draft.1/elements/id-ba1ec21bae4641378c56f714f72042d7.jsonld"}],"folder":["Application","smart-ra (base, reference copies)"]},{"id":"id-35d0806bcb5c46fab5102d75de09558f","type":"ApplicationComponent","name":"Warehouse Management System","layer":"Application","documentation":"The capabilities necessary to managing the flow of stock into the facility, its current disposition, and the flow of stock out of the facility.","properties":[{"key":"overlay:base","value":"https://litlfred.github.io/smart-ra/archimate/0.3.0-draft.1/elements/id-35d0806bcb5c46fab5102d75de09558f.jsonld"}],"folder":["Application","smart-ra (base, reference copies)"]},{"id":"id-24cc4577372e56b3a55aae9c79d58440","type":"ApplicationFunction","name":"Authentication","layer":"Application","documentation":"DHSC architecture framework, Fig. 14 (PDF 34-35)","properties":[{"key":"overlay:base","value":"https://litlfred.github.io/smart-ra/archimate/0.3.0-draft.1/elements/id-24cc4577372e56b3a55aae9c79d58440.jsonld"}],"folder":["Application","smart-ra (base, reference copies)"]},{"id":"id-a75cdd32596c5e908d01fe0cc070f8fe","type":"ApplicationFunction","name":"Encryption","layer":"Application","documentation":"DHSC architecture framework, Fig. 14 (PDF 34-35)","properties":[{"key":"overlay:base","value":"https://litlfred.github.io/smart-ra/archimate/0.3.0-draft.1/elements/id-a75cdd32596c5e908d01fe0cc070f8fe.jsonld"}],"folder":["Application","smart-ra (base, reference copies)"]},{"id":"id-a1c1c1cc41405322a68640c7d3759633","type":"ApplicationFunction","name":"Orchestration","layer":"Application","documentation":"DHSC architecture framework, Fig. 14 (PDF 34-35)","properties":[{"key":"overlay:base","value":"https://litlfred.github.io/smart-ra/archimate/0.3.0-draft.1/elements/id-a1c1c1cc41405322a68640c7d3759633.jsonld"}],"folder":["Application","smart-ra (base, reference copies)"]},{"id":"id-4d159fa30f2d55b7b754941e86eaf183","type":"ApplicationFunction","name":"Transformation","layer":"Application","documentation":"DHSC architecture framework, Fig. 14 (PDF 34-35)","properties":[{"key":"overlay:base","value":"https://litlfred.github.io/smart-ra/archimate/0.3.0-draft.1/elements/id-4d159fa30f2d55b7b754941e86eaf183.jsonld"}],"folder":["Application","smart-ra (base, reference copies)"]},{"id":"id-323e551234ce5a61a0b9c141dd314258","type":"ApplicationFunction","name":"Translation","layer":"Application","documentation":"DHSC architecture framework, Fig. 14 (PDF 34-35)","properties":[{"key":"overlay:base","value":"https://litlfred.github.io/smart-ra/archimate/0.3.0-draft.1/elements/id-323e551234ce5a61a0b9c141dd314258.jsonld"}],"folder":["Application","smart-ra (base, reference copies)"]},{"id":"id-c3d4a36bdc8c538d8be328a3adaaccb4","type":"ApplicationFunction","name":"Validation","layer":"Application","documentation":"DHSC architecture framework, Fig. 14 (PDF 34-35)","properties":[{"key":"overlay:base","value":"https://litlfred.github.io/smart-ra/archimate/0.3.0-draft.1/elements/id-c3d4a36bdc8c538d8be328a3adaaccb4.jsonld"}],"folder":["Application","smart-ra (base, reference copies)"]},{"id":"id-975c5567001151299672c0341a733111","type":"ApplicationService","name":"Product Verification","layer":"Application","documentation":"DHSC architecture framework, Fig. 14 (PDF 34-35)","properties":[{"key":"overlay:base","value":"https://litlfred.github.io/smart-ra/archimate/0.3.0-draft.1/elements/id-975c5567001151299672c0341a733111.jsonld"}],"folder":["Application","smart-ra (base, reference copies)"]},{"id":"id-65750fe0d1c65c5a846bf1de3e29f61f","type":"ApplicationService","name":"Supply Chain Reports","layer":"Application","documentation":"DHSC architecture framework, Fig. 14 (PDF 34-35)","properties":[{"key":"overlay:base","value":"https://litlfred.github.io/smart-ra/archimate/0.3.0-draft.1/elements/id-65750fe0d1c65c5a846bf1de3e29f61f.jsonld"}],"folder":["Application","smart-ra (base, reference copies)"]},{"id":"id-bc68171ed2615dad80e6f7d8199f4057","type":"ApplicationService","name":"Track and Trace","layer":"Application","documentation":"DHSC architecture framework, Fig. 14 (PDF 34-35)","properties":[{"key":"overlay:base","value":"https://litlfred.github.io/smart-ra/archimate/0.3.0-draft.1/elements/id-bc68171ed2615dad80e6f7d8199f4057.jsonld"}],"folder":["Application","smart-ra (base, reference copies)"]},{"id":"id-ce9398453f40b3d49ea2b6ede3ac24cf","type":"Grouping","name":"National Level","layer":"Other","documentation":"Health supply chain information systems run at the national (central) level (DTH SC Figs 18-19).","properties":[{"key":"overlay:owner","value":"dth-sc"}],"folder":["Other"]},{"id":"id-92084f8a38ea5db0f4f2bb90664eb27a","type":"Grouping","name":"District Level","layer":"Other","documentation":"Health supply chain information systems run at the district level (DTH SC Fig. 19).","properties":[{"key":"overlay:owner","value":"dth-sc"}],"folder":["Other"]},{"id":"id-7d5e19176af61d61219aeb1f5bef1fce","type":"Grouping","name":"Facility Level","layer":"Other","documentation":"Health supply chain information systems run at the facility level (DTH SC Figs 18-19).","properties":[{"key":"overlay:owner","value":"dth-sc"}],"folder":["Other"]},{"id":"id-65a47d9097875c88997d5f5544b388b1","type":"Grouping","name":"Analytics","layer":"Other","documentation":"DHSC architecture framework, Fig. 14 (PDF 34-35)","properties":[{"key":"overlay:base","value":"https://litlfred.github.io/smart-ra/archimate/0.3.0-draft.1/elements/id-65a47d9097875c88997d5f5544b388b1.jsonld"}],"folder":["Other","smart-ra (base, reference copies)"]},{"id":"id-a461611e13595520aa843143ef10622b","type":"Grouping","name":"Data Services","layer":"Other","documentation":"Components that support data aggregation and analysis, and traceability services that use the aggregated supply chain data to enable health product tracking, tracing and verification. (PDF 35)","properties":[{"key":"overlay:base","value":"https://litlfred.github.io/smart-ra/archimate/0.3.0-draft.1/elements/id-a461611e13595520aa843143ef10622b.jsonld"}],"folder":["Other","smart-ra (base, reference copies)"]},{"id":"id-aabf37ef1f7d546d8e801ff38cf4b6a8","type":"Grouping","name":"Digital Ecosystems","layer":"Other","documentation":"Other digital ecosystems that benefit from health supply chain data. (PDF 35)","properties":[{"key":"overlay:base","value":"https://litlfred.github.io/smart-ra/archimate/0.3.0-draft.1/elements/id-aabf37ef1f7d546d8e801ff38cf4b6a8.jsonld"}],"folder":["Other","smart-ra (base, reference copies)"]},{"id":"id-f507cb05d32a54028579c6437517150f","type":"Grouping","name":"Digital Health Supply Chain Enterprise","layer":"Other","documentation":"DHSC architecture framework, Fig. 14 (PDF 34-35)","properties":[{"key":"overlay:base","value":"https://litlfred.github.io/smart-ra/archimate/0.3.0-draft.1/elements/id-f507cb05d32a54028579c6437517150f.jsonld"}],"folder":["Other","smart-ra (base, reference copies)"]},{"id":"id-89a2f91e8b135574b8b9802bed0ad722","type":"Grouping","name":"External Systems","layer":"Other","documentation":"Systems outside the public health ecosystem that may integrate with it to exchange data, including manufacturers' systems, global platforms developed by funders or procurement agencies, and global or regional data repositories. (PDF 35)","properties":[{"key":"overlay:base","value":"https://litlfred.github.io/smart-ra/archimate/0.3.0-draft.1/elements/id-89a2f91e8b135574b8b9802bed0ad722.jsonld"}],"folder":["Other","smart-ra (base, reference copies)"]},{"id":"id-dada45a5bc1c59a186fc4acd813ab7b8","type":"Grouping","name":"Foundational Components","layer":"Other","documentation":"Components that provide system capabilities for organizing and managing master data such as product, facility and supplier data. (PDF 35)","properties":[{"key":"overlay:base","value":"https://litlfred.github.io/smart-ra/archimate/0.3.0-draft.1/elements/id-dada45a5bc1c59a186fc4acd813ab7b8.jsonld"}],"folder":["Other","smart-ra (base, reference copies)"]},{"id":"id-ef2ed03c5fd958cbae67247b253bcba0","type":"Grouping","name":"Health Supply Chain Information Systems","layer":"Other","documentation":"These systems support the various supply chain processes. One system or digital platform might support one or more supply chain processes. (PDF 35)","properties":[{"key":"overlay:base","value":"https://litlfred.github.io/smart-ra/archimate/0.3.0-draft.1/elements/id-ef2ed03c5fd958cbae67247b253bcba0.jsonld"}],"folder":["Other","smart-ra (base, reference copies)"]},{"id":"id-3398a2d96e915055bf5e7aef22f9fbf8","type":"Grouping","name":"Interoperability Layer","layer":"Other","documentation":"This component facilitates the exchange of data across various systems as well as across levels of the health system. (PDF 35)","properties":[{"key":"overlay:base","value":"https://litlfred.github.io/smart-ra/archimate/0.3.0-draft.1/elements/id-3398a2d96e915055bf5e7aef22f9fbf8.jsonld"}],"folder":["Other","smart-ra (base, reference copies)"]},{"id":"id-43460361d71e57d2b0bb644b1ac6904d","type":"Grouping","name":"Shared Services","layer":"Other","documentation":"DHSC architecture framework, Fig. 14 (PDF 34-35)","properties":[{"key":"overlay:base","value":"https://litlfred.github.io/smart-ra/archimate/0.3.0-draft.1/elements/id-43460361d71e57d2b0bb644b1ac6904d.jsonld"}],"folder":["Other","smart-ra (base, reference copies)"]},{"id":"id-65d5884fa08c526e91d56c6f8a2f6391","type":"Grouping","name":"Traceability","layer":"Other","documentation":"DHSC architecture framework, Fig. 14 (PDF 34-35)","properties":[{"key":"overlay:base","value":"https://litlfred.github.io/smart-ra/archimate/0.3.0-draft.1/elements/id-65d5884fa08c526e91d56c6f8a2f6391.jsonld"}],"folder":["Other","smart-ra (base, reference copies)"]}],"relationships":[],"views":[{"id":"id-ab7ddf2e88d786e2f3b40bd251b1ed71","name":"Maturity-based Architecture: SCISMM Level 3 to Level 4 (DTH SC Fig. 15)","documentation":"Fig. 15 (PDF 36): the framework without external systems and digital ecosystems. As printed, both data-service groups are labelled \"Foundational components\" (Figs 14 and 16-19 name them Analytics and Traceability). Groupings and members as drawn; no relationships beyond membership are asserted.","folder":["Views"]},{"id":"id-fa02287de9e115eac00f1c5feb4fca0c","name":"Maturity-based Architecture: SCISMM Level 4 to Level 5 (DTH SC Fig. 16)","documentation":"Fig. 16 (PDF 37): the full framework, interoperating with digital ecosystems and external systems. Groupings and members as drawn; no relationships beyond membership are asserted.","folder":["Views"]},{"id":"id-e98b3f0767571507b2113b33342ed0db","name":"Supply Chain Design: Centralized Management (DTH SC Fig. 17)","documentation":"Fig. 17 (PDF 38): SCISMM Level 5; all supply chain services are centrally managed, as in Fig. 14. Groupings and members as drawn; no relationships beyond membership are asserted.","folder":["Views"]},{"id":"id-548ef5cca9e14b658dd086a42f0440c5","name":"Supply Chain Design: Decentralized Management, Option A (DTH SC Fig. 18)","documentation":"Fig. 18 (PDF 39): SCISMM Level 5; the supply chain systems split between the national level and the facility level. Groupings and members as drawn; no relationships beyond membership are asserted.","folder":["Views"]},{"id":"id-2ddd2da649fce7285cf1b7f4dfe0f954","name":"Supply Chain Design: Decentralized Management, Option B (DTH SC Fig. 19)","documentation":"Fig. 19 (PDF 40): SCISMM Level 5; districts procure apart from the central level. The figure draws order, inventory and cold chain management on the district/facility boundary; the view places them between the two levels. Groupings and members as drawn; no relationships beyond membership are asserted.","folder":["Views"]}],"inViews":{"id-f507cb05d32a54028579c6437517150f":["id-ab7ddf2e88d786e2f3b40bd251b1ed71","id-fa02287de9e115eac00f1c5feb4fca0c","id-e98b3f0767571507b2113b33342ed0db","id-548ef5cca9e14b658dd086a42f0440c5","id-2ddd2da649fce7285cf1b7f4dfe0f954"],"id-43460361d71e57d2b0bb644b1ac6904d":["id-ab7ddf2e88d786e2f3b40bd251b1ed71","id-fa02287de9e115eac00